## Why This Is Asked
The barrier tests fundamental atomic sequencing and memory-order choices without OS primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Barrier reuse with generation counter
- Atomic increments and acquire/release semantics
- False sharing avoidance via padding
- Stress testing for thread skew and latency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo:
volatile int arrivals; // atomic
volatile int generation; // atomic

void barrier_enter(int N) {
  int a = atomic_fetch_add_explicit(&arrivals, 1, memory_order_acq_rel);
  if (a + 1 == N) {
    atomic_store_explicit(&arrivals, 0, memory_order_relaxed);
    atomic_fetch_add_explicit(&generation, 1, memory_order_release);
  }
  int g = atomic_load_explicit(&generation, memory_order_acquire);
  while (g == atomic_load_explicit(&generation, memory_order_acquire)) { ; }
}
```

